; TS2Python.def — force undecorated export names for EL's DefineDLLFunc.
;
; Why: on x86 with __stdcall + __declspec(dllexport), MSVC decorates exports
; as _Name@N (e.g. _EL_Init@4). EasyLanguage's DefineDLLFunc / GetProcAddress
; looks up the raw "EL_Init" name and fails. Listing exports here makes the
; linker emit them under the plain symbol name while keeping the __stdcall
; call convention intact.
;
; Keep this in sync with include/ts2python.h.
;
; EL_PublishTick and EL_PublishBar are TOMBSTONES — they return -6 and
; publish nothing. Keep them listed: dropping an export makes an .ELD built
; against the superseded protocol fail at DefineDLLFunc resolution with no
; explanation, whereas -6 puts a readable line in TradeStation's Print Log.
; See ../contract/error_codes.md.
;
; The init export is EL_InitChart. EL_Init is a TOMBSTONE at the superseded
; protocol's ONE-parameter signature, and EL_Init2 / EL_Init3 stay gone.
;
; A revision of this DLL reused the name EL_Init for the five-parameter init.
; __stdcall has the callee pop the arguments, so a stale .ELD resolved it,
; called it with one argument against five, and corrupted the stack — no error
; code, nothing on this side able to detect it. Renaming restores the guard:
; a stale .ELD now lands on the one-parameter tombstone and reads -6, and a
; current .ELD against an older DLL finds no EL_InitChart and fails at Verify.
;
; The DLL and the .ELD are still one unit — install and re-Verify together.

LIBRARY TS2Python
EXPORTS
    EL_InitChart
    EL_Init
    EL_Publish
    EL_PublishTick
    EL_PublishBar
    EL_Shutdown
    EL_DllVersion
